    "body": "I think that we should add a note here that explains how it's possible for constructor url to be equal but constructor origin to be different. Something like: \"The reason we compare both constructor url and constructor origin is that data: URLs cause the created worker settings object to have a unique opaque origin, instead of one derived from the constructor url. This ensures that using the same data: URL multiple times creates separate SharedWorkerGlobalScope instances, as desired.\" (Hope I got that right...)\n",
